# =============================================================================
# Sampling visuals as slide images (for a "build-up" animation in PowerPoint)
#
# Goal shown to students: estimate the % of target-coloured balls in a jar
# from a sample. Produces PNG images, all the same size (16:9) with everything
# in the same position, so pasting them onto consecutive slides makes
# "Next slide" look like an animation.
#
#   slide1_frame01.png  jar + text only
#   slide1_frame02.png  + sample #1 of n = 5   (its balls circled in the jar)
#   slide1_frame03.png  + sample #2
#   slide1_frame04.png  + sample #3
#   slide1_frame05.png  all 30 samples of n = 5
#   slide1_frame06.png  + all 30 of n = 10
#   slide1_frame07.png  + all 30 of n = 15
#   slide1_frame08.png  + all 30 of n = 20   (the full page)
#   slide2.png          worked example for n = 5
#   slide3.png          summary table
#   all_slides.pdf      every frame above, in order (handy to check the flow)
#
# Everything is saved in your working directory: getwd().
# The script also PRINTS all the numbers in the console, stores them in a list
# called `results`, and (in RStudio / interactive R) draws every page in the
# Plots pane so you can flip through them with the arrows.
#
# PowerPoint tip: insert each PNG full-slide (13.333 x 7.5 in) on its own
# slide, same position; use no transition (or "Fade", 0.3 s) between frames.
#
# Base R only (grid + grDevices). Nothing to install.
# The jar and all 120 samples are fixed below, so every run is identical.
# All counts / % / means are computed from those balls and checked.
# =============================================================================

library(grid)

